// Policy: 13_rate_limit_destructive_actions   (Dogwood temporal policy)
// Category: Defense in depth
// Intent: Refuse a sixth terminate_instance call within one hour of the
//         same policy session. The count includes the current request.
//         One temporal policy per action keeps the syntax to the form the
//         author tested; copy it for delete_resource (quota: 20 temporal
//         policies per engine, 3 temporal operators per policy).
//
// Trusted input: the session's own event history, recorded by AgentCore
//   Policy. Nothing upstream has to compute a counter.
// Requirements:
//   - every request carries x-amzn-bedrock-agentcore-policy-session-id, and
//     YOUR BACKEND chooses that ID (e.g. HMAC(user, conversation)). If the
//     agent picks it, a new ID resets the count. In the author's 2026-10-12
//     lab, rotating the ID defeated a per-session limit in 20 of 20 trials.
//   - the Gateway role needs bedrock-agentcore:GetWorkloadAccessToken.
//   - a permit for these actions must exist (policy 02); create it before
//     this forbid or strict validation may report "Overly Restrictive".
// Counting ::request means denied attempts count too (40 of 40 trials in the
//   same lab). For a destructive limit I want that: an agent hammering a
//   denied delete should lock itself out. Count ::response instead if only
//   completed calls should count (untested by the author).
// 2nd edition change: the 1st edition read
//   context.input.destructive_count_last_hour from an "upstream authorizer".
//   No authorizer in front of the user API can write into tool arguments.
// Local testing: cedarpy cannot parse Dogwood. CI submits this file with
//   definition={"policy": {...}} and validates it on AWS only.

forbid (
  principal,
  action == AgentCore::Action::"devops-prod___terminate_instance",
  resource == AgentCore::Gateway::"arn:aws:bedrock-agentcore:REGION:ACCOUNT:gateway/GATEWAY_ID"
)
when temporal {
  exists (n: Long).
    (count for (t: Timepoint).
      where (formerly within 1h (
        AgentCore::Action::"devops-prod___terminate_instance"::request{ eventResource: resource }
        && tp(t)))) == n
    && n > 5
};
